cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ThinkModel — an open-source curriculum for AI literacy"
message: >-
  If you teach from this curriculum, translate it, or adapt it, please cite it.
  Attribution is what CC BY 4.0 asks for in return, and a citation is the
  easiest way to give it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Abulaila
    given-names: Amer
repository-code: "https://github.com/aabulaila/ThinkModel-content"
url: "https://thinkmodel.ai"
abstract: >-
  Two complete AI literacy courses totalling 25 units and roughly 69,000 words,
  written for adults and teenagers with no technical background. Course 101
  covers how AI works, why it fails, and how to use it well. Course 102 covers
  operating AI systems: workspaces, agents, autonomy, security, and automation.
keywords:
  - AI literacy
  - curriculum
  - open educational resources
  - artificial intelligence
  - education
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-08-11"
version: "1.0.0"
